// Building types (docs/game_design.md §5.1-5.5). The id is also the sprite name.
//
// Fields (optional ones have defaults):
//   id, name, plural (German plural; required for buildings that shoot, texts count them),
//   description, category (Housing | Production | Agriculture | Public | Military),
//   size: (width, depth) in tiles, cost: (gold, materials: {resource: amount}),
//   build_hours (construction work for one builder), workers, job: (category, tier),
//   upkeep (gold/day), buildable (false = only reachable by upgrading), material (Wood | Stone),
//   upgrade: (to, cost, hours) — next level; cost and hours default to the target's construction
//   cost and build_hours; the building keeps workers, stock, buffers, recipes and orders,
//   outdoor (work outside: weather changes the work speed, doc §8.2),
//   role (General | Headquarters | TradeHub | WallSegment | Gate),
//   access (Entrance | AnySide) — AnySide (1x1, no storage): walkers enter from any walkable
//   neighbour tile, the entrance first, and the construction site needs no road (walls, gates,
//   towers on a wall line; doc §5.5),
//   production: (gathering, recipes: [(id, name, inputs, optional_inputs, outputs, hours)],
//                uses_tools, buffer), housing: (capacity, tier, class, tax_per_resident,
//   income_per_worker (household earnings per working member and day, doc §6),
//   requires: (needs, services, goods: [[any of]])), services: [(kind, radius)],
//   storage: (capacity_per_resource, accepts, carrier_radius), sells, territory_radius,
//   garrison (soldiers stationed inside), defense: (ranged, range, hit_points) — shots per
//   combat round at enemies within `range` tiles and the structure's hit points (without it:
//   military.building_hp_per_tile per footprint tile, doc §11),
//   placement: [MaxCount | NearWater | NearDeposit | OnWallLine].
//
// Which technology unlocks a building is defined ONLY in technologies.ron (UnlockBuilding);
// buildings not unlocked by any technology are available from the start.
// Upgrading a house costs the construction cost of the target tier (houses name no upgrade cost).
#![enable(implicit_some)]
[
    // =======================================================================================
    // 5.1 Wohngebäude
    // =======================================================================================
